From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] session-lock-qt: load private target from public component

License: Apache-2.0
Upstream-Status: downstream-only
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

openEuler Qt 6.5 exports Qt6::WaylandClientPrivate from the public
Qt6WaylandClientConfig.cmake file. It does not ship a separate
Qt6WaylandClientPrivateConfig.cmake, so requesting WaylandClientPrivate as a
component fails before the exported private target can be used.

Load the public WaylandClient component, which imports both targets, while
continuing to link Qt6::WaylandClientPrivate. This retains all Wayland
session-lock functionality and private API use.

Remove this patch when upstream no longer requests WaylandClientPrivate as a
separate component, or when the target distribution provides a separate
Qt6WaylandClientPrivateConfig.cmake.

---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -30,4 +30,4 @@
 find_package(Qt6 REQUIRED COMPONENTS Core Gui WaylandClient
-             WaylandClientPrivate Qml Quick)
+             Qml Quick)
 find_package(Qt6WaylandScannerTools REQUIRED)
 find_package(WaylandScanner REQUIRED)
